# Site shell vs AI

PocketEdge is a full product (News, Research, Portfolio, Advisors, Resources, AI). `/ai` is one section, not a separate app.

- Always keep `SiteHeader` and mobile `BottomNav` on `/ai`. Do not hide them for “immersive” chat, live conversations, or agent threads.
- AI UI lives inside `AppShell` `main` — below the header, above the bottom nav.
- Every desktop page uses the same chrome as `/ai`: full-bleed header (logo in the rail column, section title, account) and the product left rail (News, Research, Ask AI, Portfolio, Advisors, Resources). Do not put those links back in a centered header.
- The agent roster sits under that product nav on every desktop page. It is a list, so it stays visible while the user reads News, Research, or anything else. Highlight the active agent only on `/ai`.
- Desktop left rail is sticky under the header (`top-14`, height `100dvh - 3.5rem`). Mobile keeps BottomNav and the AI inbox; do not show this rail there.
- Files / connections belong in the right context rail or demoted footer, not as primary left-rail destinations.
- Do not invent a parallel IA inside AI that ignores the rest of the product.
